ing is obviously really  tricky we all know the back story that  the time in New York didn't go well and  and really it seemed like you know  Mike's coaching career was going to be  going down a dark road at that point  because of the conflicts that he had  with Melo stylistically you know he  wanted a plan was a stretch for Melo  didn't want to do it they just didn't  mesh well so I don't know who they're  kind of you know taking aim at  specifically I just think that these  guys are brothers to Melo they are  extremely tight with him and it's not  even just a banana boat crew I just saw  Damian Lillard was you know saying the  same thing saying you gotta keep some  respect on Melos name but you know I  don't know I just think it's hard  for those guys to see his name kind of  get dragged through the mud like this  but he's not playing well and he's not  the same guy he was a few years ago so  if he's bought out and sent sent into  free agency if you will Sam can LeBron  go and grab his buddy  in the same way I know obviously Tyson  Chandler's a much better fit as we've  seen with them not losing since  acquiring him what do you think I could  see it yeah I mean it's funny because I  was in the Lakers locker room two nights  ago when they rolled through Sacramento  and this story was just starting to  surface I even talked to a Lakers  official just casually about it and the  idea of you know what do you think Melo  maybe wearing the purple and gold  sometime soon and you know and the  conversation didn't go any further than  then kind of all both of us stating the  obvious that you know that LeBron Melo  connection is front and center and if  not there then we're because we've  already seen you know Magic Johnson's  willingness to put as many you know  characters in that locker room as  possible and Melo in that regard and I'm  not even trying to be flippant with it  but in terms of just taking calculated  risks with you know players that other  places have given 