ich adding covington  i think they fit better than you know  some of the other names that were part  of the discussion but philly was the  team that was laying in the weeds they  had pulled out of it weeks and weeks ago  and as of Wednesday I was told  essentially kind of put there  take it or leave a type offer on the  table and then the Wolves had to think  about it and then you know that game  against the Kings obviously with a  tipping point it was so ugly one five  road trip you know Jimmy's play really  inconsistent that night so many weird  vibes around the team and they kind of  grabbed that deal off the table so when  it all comes down to it Sam with the  Warriors tonight taking on the Clippers  without Steph and without draymond Green  who do you think has the best chance in  the West to be this year's Rockets to  use potentially an injury an injury  marred stretch for the Warriors to  leapfrog them in the standings should  that at all be feasible what do you  think right well I mean the crazy part  is that all of a sudden I mean somebody  in the West obviously is gonna try and  try to take that Rockets role but the  East have it you know I'm getting a lot  more interesting maybe the finals would  be more compelling than they have been  last couple of years but if I got a pick  a team I mean I'll probably give it to  Utah you know they've been inconsistent  early on but I love their formula and  and you know that's a team now that with  Donovan in the second year Rudy Gobert  you know becoming you know reigning  these kinds of player of the year and I  love their coaching staff and you know  they're gonna probably do something at  the trade deadline in February to  they've got a very  a forward-thinking front office so the  Jazz is you know if you ask me which  kind of programs I trust the most it's  probably Utah interests um and you know  beyond that there's compelling teams out  there I mean Denver's looked great so  far  Portland's won four in a row and they  come in and take on a Lakers team to try  and send the Lakers hurtling back to 500  on Wednesday that's right that I think  they can do and they probably will do  I'm not buying the Lakers yet I'm the  decent team I'm not buying them as being  able to push back against Portland and  the Blazers on the one hand I give them  a kind of credit you know I did a long  interview with Damian Lillard going into  the season where you know I always  believed in Damian and his like fabric  and fiber I just kind of looked at the  rest of the roster and I saw like coming  off a sweep against New Orleans in the  first round last year I had a hard time  processing that idea that it could  really bounce back and be a top-tier  team again and they've done that they  look great but matchup wise you know the  Warriors I mean the Warriors give  everybody fit the rosters are the Bucks  are the Blazers roster is just not built  well I don't think in relation to the  Warriors so I don't see them as a  Rockets type of threat at all the Rich  Eisen show weekdays at noon eastern on  audience

